/-! # Finite-degree descent of an ideal from an algebraic-space blowup

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors on Spaces, Tags 0860 and 085M
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-blowup-finite-degree-ideal-descent).

Images below are categorical images in module sheaves. Products use the existing
locally generated ideal-power sections, so the equality is an equality of ideal
subsheaves on every etale test, including nonaffine tests.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- Every finite-type ideal on a finite-type blowup of a qcqs algebraic space descends
from a finite-type ideal contained in a positive power of the centre, after multiplying
by the corresponding power of the exceptional ideal. No reducedness or density is assumed.
Source: Stacks Project, Divisors on Spaces, Tag 0860, finite-degree choice and the final
chart calculation, using Tag 085M; the ideal equality is on the first blowup
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-blowup-finite-degree-ideal-descent).

Proof:
1. Form the quasi-coherent Rees algebra A = directSum I^n. Quasi-coherence of powers
   follows from tensor multiplication and images by lem-sfb-space-qcoh-affine-chart-calculus,
   and that of the sum by lem-sfb-space-qcoh-kernels-colimits. The blowup projection is
   proper, hence quasi-compact, by lem-sfb-space-blowup-chart-properties. By
   lem-sfb-space-ideal-closed-subspace-correspondence, J defines a closed subspace Z of
   the blowup; lem-sfb-space-closed-structure-finite-presentation makes it finitely presented.
2. Apply lem-sfb-space-proj-finite-degree-equations to obtain d > 0 and a finite-type
   quasi-coherent submodule F of A_d = I^d cutting out Z in Proj(A). Its inclusion into
   O_T makes F a finite-type quasi-coherent ideal H contained in I^d.
3. On an affine etale chart Spec R of T, put M = H(Spec R). By
   lem-sfb-space-relative-proj-scheme-tests and
   lem-sfb-space-relative-proj-quotient-closed-immersion, Z restricts to Proj(A/(MA)).
   The blowup is covered by Spec R[I/a] for a in I, by
   lem-sfb-space-blowup-chart-properties. Identify this chart with D_+(a t) using
   prop-nagata-proj-standard-open, prop-nagata-affine-blowup-chart, and
   def-nagata-homogeneous-away-to-chart. The closed ideal restricts to J by the
   base-change clause of lem-sfb-space-ideal-closed-subspace-correspondence.
4. By lem-sfb-graded-proj-quotient-twist-comparison, the ideal on D_+(f), f = a t,
   is the kernel of A_(f) -> (A/(MA))_(f). A kernel fraction b/f^n has f^k b in MA
   for some k, by def-nagata-homogeneous-localization-degree-zero. Increase k so
   n+k >= d and write f^k b = sum m_j c_j with m_j in M and c_j of degree n+k-d.
   Then b/f^n = sum (m_j/f^d)(c_j/f^(n+k-d)). Conversely every m/f^d is in the
   kernel. Thus the ideal of Z on Spec R[I/a] is generated by m/a^d for m in M.
   The same calculation includes nilpotent f and zero localized rings.
5. On R[I/a], the extended centre ideal is (a), and the image of m is a^d(m/a^d).
   Consequently M R[I/a] = (a)^d J. The tensor formula of
   def-trf-space-etale-module-functors identifies these extended ideals with the
   images of the canonical tensor maps. Products agree with the ordinary chart
   products. The charts cover the blowup, so both local inclusions descend to the
   asserted equality of ideal subsheaves. No cancellation or density is used. -/
theorem exists_finiteDegree_ideal_blowupPresentation
    {S : Scheme.{u}} (T : AlgebraicSpace S)
    (hqc : ∃ (V : Over S) (a : yoneda.obj V ⟶ T.obj.obj),
      CompactSpace V.left ∧ IsEtale a ∧ IsSurjective a)
    (hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated T)
    (I : QuasiCoherentIdeal T) (hI : (I.val : T.Modules).IsFiniteType)
    (B : BlowupPresentation I)
    (J : QuasiCoherentIdeal B.space) (hJ : (J.val : B.space.Modules).IsFiniteType) :
    ∃ (d : ℕ), 0 < d ∧ ∃ (H : QuasiCoherentIdeal T),
      (H.val : T.Modules).IsFiniteType ∧
      (∀ V : T.EtaleSite,
        Set.range (H.val.arrow.val.app (op V)) ⊆
          idealPowerSubsheafSections I.val.arrow (SheafOfModules.unit T.structureSheaf)
            (fun _ ↦ Set.univ) d V) ∧
      ∀ V : B.space.EtaleSite,
        Set.range ((image.ι (idealTensorMap B.projection H)).val.app (op V)) =
          idealPowerSubsheafSections (image.ι (idealTensorMap B.projection I))
            (SheafOfModules.unit B.space.structureSheaf)
            (fun W ↦ Set.range (J.val.arrow.val.app (op W))) d V := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
